@title rast — SIMD raster tile processing for Erlang
@version 0.1.0
@copyright 2026 Steve Roques
@doc

== Overview ==

rast processes large satellite raster scenes (Sentinel-2 / Landsat) on the BEAM
using fused, typed, binary-first SIMD tile kernels under a bounded-memory OTP
tiling layer.

Two layers:

<ul>
  <li><b>Kernels</b> ({@link rast_nif}, façade {@link rast}) — bounded per-tile
      operations in Rust. Binary-first, fused, and typed (`u16 -&gt; f32'
      widening folded into the kernel).</li>
  <li><b>Orchestration</b> ({@link rast_coordinator}, {@link rast_worker},
      {@link rast_gdal}) — demand-driven tiling of a whole scene under a fixed
      memory budget, with GDAL doing windowed I/O. Skeleton in this release.</li>
</ul>

Pure tile geometry lives in {@link rast_tiling}.

== Design ==

See `ARCHITECTURE.md' at the ecosystem root for the full rationale: why the API
is binary-first, why kernels are fused and typed, the Erlang/Rust boundary, the
tiling/backpressure strategy, multi-arch dispatch, and the incremental plan.

@end
